WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.670
- [Atari] Eight pork products crammed into one

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.193
huge pork patty.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.070
^- What's up internet, I'm the sauce boss

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:07.020
^from Epic Meal Time.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.180
^I'm here with my boy.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.093
^- Chef Atari.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:10.330
Today we're going to be baking

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:11.770
the power pork patty,

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:13.610
but a little toned down, scaled down version

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.860
that you can make in your home, in your small ovens.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:16.750
And we didn't stop there,

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.680
we bacon wrapped that, in a bacon weave.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.090
- [Harley] Let's make it happen.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.140
So the power pork patty's special because

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.960
when you're constantly thinking up recipes,

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.350
we always have to reach into the deepest,

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:31.733
darkest corners of what could be, or should be a meal.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.240
- [Atari] Everybody's always like, oh my god,

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.900
I must eat an epic meal, oh my god.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.530
Then you put them in front of an epic meal,

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:38.010
they don't even know what to do with it,

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.470
like they don't even know their first bite,

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:40.780
or how to even approach it,

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:41.963
and it's like exactly.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.030
People sometimes just get a little scared,

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.810
or a little shocked at how big

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.510
these larger than life meals are.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:49.580
- [Harley] Epic Meal Time's always been about innovation

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:52.510
and, I saw in the Food Game, there are just lots of meals

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:53.930
that can be taken to the next level,

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:55.960
that weren't being taken to the next level.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.810
Whenever I have a crazy idea,

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:58.960
I go up to Atari and I'm like,

00:00:58.960 --> 00:00:59.793
let's make it happen.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.040
He's like, it sounds impossible,

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.253
and I'm like well, that's your job.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:06.963
And he makes it happen, he makes the impossible possible.

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:09.070
- [Atari] We call ourselves Google chefs.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:10.430
We see it, we look at it,

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:12.280
and we multiply the hell out of it.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.230
So my role on Epic Meal Time

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:17.003
is bacon manipulation, transformation engineer.

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:18.470
- [Harley] Once we first started out,

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:20.800
it was just like we were just joking around,

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.590
and having a good time, but then there were,

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:25.030
you know, leading minds in the culinary world

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:27.233
looking to us to see what we were doing.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.330
We have now become the forefront

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:31.150
of ridiculous neo concepts.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:33.770
- [Akira] Being a guerrilla chef, cooking unconventionally,

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:35.660
is the science, there's never really

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:38.403
a right or wrong way to cook, so just go for it.

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.580
I never thought I'd be cooking an ostrich egg

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:42.990
on the side of Arnold Schwarzenegger's tank.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.700
We made the steak and egger sandwich,

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.103
steak and egger.

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.300
- [Harley] Pure pork deliciousness.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:50.910
There's like a personal pork patty.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:51.800
It's too powerful.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:53.710
You've got that sweetness from the ham in there,

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:55.640
saltiness from the sausage, mmm.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.360
- Yep, that's a mini power pork patty.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.630
- Feels delicious in my power pork palate.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:01.527
- [Atari] Oh yes.

00:02:02.409 --> 00:02:04.826
(epic music)

